% -s sorts each query's rows on their own rather than the whole output at
% once (PLAN.md §14.3), so the blank line between two result blocks stays
% where it belongs: a single sort over everything would merge the blocks and
% carry the separator off with the rows.  Both relations are stored in an
% order sorting has to undo.
edge(c, a).
edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).

name(c, gamma).
name(a, alpha).
name(b, beta).

edge(X, Y)?
name(P, N)?
